<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame frame--creed">
    <p class="kicker">Closing stance</p>
    <p class="lede">The inverted torus tells a state how to return. The wormhole must tell spacetime how to
      let it pass.</p>
    <p>That distinction gives the conjecture a useful shape. Global monodromy can remain a topological model;
      a localised throat becomes a gravitational research programme. If the programme cannot supply energy,
      stability, causality and a discriminating observation, the honest result is not a hidden portal. It is
      an orientation-reversing map and no more.</p>
    <p class="muted small">Read the global construction in
      <a href="/inverted-toruses/">The Universe of Inverted Tori</a>, the underlying transition in
      <a href="/moebius/">the Möbius seam</a>, the horizon account in <a href="/seams/">Seams</a>, and the
      round-trip question in <a href="/double-inversion/">Two Inversions</a>.</p>
  </div>
</section>
